# sidgwick over the corpus's shared atoms, written by phil/corpus from readings/sidgwick/logic: not to be edited
atom	desired	each person, so far as he believes it to be attainable, desires his own happiness
atom	proof	we have all the proof which the case admits of that happiness is a good
atom	own_good	each person's happiness is a good to that person
atom	general_good	the general happiness is a good to the aggregate of all persons
atom	end_of_conduct	happiness has made out its title as one of the ends of conduct
atom	criterion	happiness is one of the criteria of morality
atom	sidgwick_general_desirable	the general happiness is desirable, i.e. what each individual ought to desire or aim at realising in action
atom	sidgwick_actual_desire_general	there is an actual desire for the general happiness
atom	sidgwick_individual_desire_general	an actual desire for the general happiness exists in some individual
atom	sidgwick_aggregate_desire_general	an actual desire for the general happiness exists in an aggregate of individuals
atom	sidgwick_established	Mill's reasoning establishes that the general happiness is desirable
atom	sidgwick_gap_filled	the gap in Mill's expressed argument is filled
atom	sidgwick_rational_benevolence	some such proposition as the intuition of Rational Benevolence is supplied
P1	S7	sidgwick_established → sidgwick_actual_desire_general	says mill
P2	S8	desired	says mill	kind empirical
P3	S9	desired → proof	says mill
P4	S9	proof → own_good	says mill
P5	S9	own_good → general_good	says mill
P6	S12	sidgwick_actual_desire_general → sidgwick_general_desirable
P7	S12	sidgwick_established → sidgwick_actual_desire_general
P8	S13	¬sidgwick_individual_desire_general	kind conceptual
P9	S13	¬sidgwick_individual_desire_general → ¬sidgwick_aggregate_desire_general
A1	-	sidgwick_actual_desire_general → sidgwick_individual_desire_general ∨ sidgwick_aggregate_desire_general
C1	S14	¬sidgwick_actual_desire_general	from P8 P9 A1
P10	S14	sidgwick_gap_filled → sidgwick_rational_benevolence
C	S14	¬sidgwick_established	from C1 P7
